# Auto detect text files and perform LF normalization
* text=auto

# The visual-regression baselines under e2e/ are real binary image files and are
# tracked in git, so they must be excluded from `text=auto` explicitly. Git's own
# binary sniffing already catches most of these, but it works by looking for NUL
# bytes. That sniff is exactly what must not be trusted here: a baseline whose
# header is damaged could be classified as text, and `text=auto` would then rewrite
# its line endings on checkout, silently corrupting the very pixels the comparison
# asserts on. Naming the formats removes the guesswork.
#
# Scoped to the snapshot directory rather than declared as `*.png` etc. so that adding
# a real SVG or PNG source asset to `src/` later keeps normal text handling.
e2e/export/visual-regression.spec.ts-snapshots/** binary

# Playwright HTML reports embed large base64 blobs on few lines; normalizing them is
# pure churn. They are gitignored, so this only affects locally generated files.
playwright-report/** -text
blob-report/** -text
